  "name": "Azure Key Vault",
  "label": "Azure Key Vault data-plane REST",
  "description": "Azure Key Vault data-plane REST (api-version 7.6 default; 7.4 still accepted) via OfficialApiNode. Docs: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/rest/api/keyvault/secrets/get-secret/get-secret?view=rest-keyvault-secrets-7.6. Operations: get-secret, set-secret, delete-secret, list-secrets, get-key, encrypt, decrypt, get-certificate, listen. Auth secret access_token is instance config only (never on INPUT, never logged). GET/access operations still call the official GET (or access) HTTP method. Retrieved secret material must not be logged and should stay in StudioQuack secret bindings (bind OUTPUT `data` into a secret; do not print it, persist it in engine variables, or leave it on a logged edge). listen is kind:ingress — use a BPMN message start/catch/boundary event. JDK HTTP, official API only. Errors raise a BPMN error for the error boundary event (INVALID_INPUT, AUTH_FAILED, RATE_LIMITED, HTTP_<status>, REQUEST_FAILED); secrets are redacted.",
  "icon": "lock",
